  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA ridge of high pressure builds over the Southwest US and then \nslides towards the Southeast US mid to late week. Meanwhile, the \nMiddle Ohio Valley will be entrenched within a west to northwest \nflow regime on the periphery of this ridge. Amidst this pattern, a \nseries of mesoscale convective systems are projected to traverse the \narea, bringing rounds of strong to severe thunderstorms as well as \npotential for substantial flash flooding. \n\nWhile both the timing and track of these systems are uncertain, \nthere is high confidence that the systems will bring impactful \nweather to the area today through Thursday.\n\n- Flooding:\n\nPlenty of moisture, evidenced by precipitable water values in the \n1.5 to 2 inch range, will support heavy downpours within any \nconvection that develops this week. These downpours could easily \nproduce an inch or two of rain in a short amount of time. Training \nstorms would produce even higher amounts that could result in flash \nflooding. The flood risk may be further heightened as systems \ncontinue to roll through over the next couple of days.\n\nAlthough there is low confidence in where highest rainfall amounts \nwill accrue, there is high confidence that there will be enough rain \nfor flooding to develop in the area. Should \"worst case\" model \nscenarios materialize, then significant flooding would be \npossible for portions of the area. In addition to the flash \nflood threat, river flooding may develop as excessive rainfall \nmakes its way into local streams and rivers.\n\nA Flood Watch has been issued for the entirety of the forecast area \nfrom this afternoon through Thursday night. \n\n- Severe Thunderstorms:\n\nThe aforementioned convective systems are also expected to \nusher rounds of strong to severe thunderstorms across the area\nthis week. Damaging winds will be the primary concern, though \nthe environment could also support a low-end tornado threat, or\npotential for marginally severe hail.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA ridge of high pressure strengthens over the southeast US, \nprompting quieter weather late week into the weekend; however,\nthis reprieve is likely to be short-lived as the ridge is \nprojected to break down or shift west again early in the new \nwork week.",
